WEBVTT

00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:16,820
If your numbers for your AST, ALT and GGT are good, does that mean the liver is detoxed

00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:18,820
at a good shape?

00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:21,820
No, it doesn't.

00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:28,820
Remember, your blood tests just give you clues, and they really give you clues of healthy

00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:30,820
function or dysfunction.

00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:36,820
And it can take a lot of dysfunction before those numbers get out of balance.

00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:39,820
I would never say your blood all looks good.

00:00:39,820 --> 00:00:41,820
Your liver numbers look good.

00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:44,820
That means your liver is all detoxed.

00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:46,820
Your liver is constantly detoxified.

00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:50,820
If you're not detoxified, you are toxified and you're getting sicker.

00:00:50,820 --> 00:00:58,820
So even if a person is a slow detoxifier, let's say their liver is not doing...

00:00:58,820 --> 00:01:04,820
Let's say their liver is damaged and it's only functioning at, you know,

00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:07,820
35% of its function.

00:01:07,820 --> 00:01:10,820
You can still have normal AST and ALT and GGT.

00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:14,820
Your liver is just only going to function at 35% of its function.

00:01:14,820 --> 00:01:20,820
So your toxins that are circulating in your blood are going to be deposited in your

00:01:20,820 --> 00:01:30,820
extracellular spaces and probably be stored in extracellular fat cells and other cells.

00:01:31,820 --> 00:01:34,820
Your liver can store toxins.

00:01:34,820 --> 00:01:42,820
And if your liver is damaged, you can't have elevated AST, ALT,

00:01:42,820 --> 00:01:44,820
alkaline phosphatase, etc.

00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:49,820
But, you know, your liver can be functioning far less than it should

00:01:49,820 --> 00:01:53,820
and you could be very toxic in those numbers, it'd be normal.

00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:57,820
So I wouldn't say that the liver is detoxed and in good shape.

00:01:57,820 --> 00:02:01,820
Just because I have good numbers, we don't know all of that.

00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:03,820
We don't know that for sure.

